window.ENGLISH_CARDS = [{"kind":"phrase","front":"play it by ear","meaning":"走一步看一步；根据情况调整（不一定完全没计划）","example":"We can decide where to eat later. Let's play it by ear."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a close call","meaning":"险些出事；差一点就……","example":"I nearly missed the train. That was a close call."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put a damper on something","meaning":"给心情、兴致、计划泼冷水","example":"The rain put a damper on our weekend plans."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get carried away","meaning":"一时上头；做过头","example":"I got carried away and spent way too much."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be on the fence (about)","meaning":"对某事犹豫不决","example":"I'm still on the fence about joining the trip."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"come in handy","meaning":"派上用场","example":"A power bank might come in handy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"work around something","meaning":"想办法克服限制／变通处理","example":"We can work around your schedule."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"catch someone off guard","meaning":"让人措手不及","example":"His question caught me off guard."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make the most of","meaning":"尽量充分利用","example":"Let's make the most of the good weather."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"call it a day","meaning":"收工；今天到此为止","example":"We're exhausted. Let's call it a day."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"wing it","meaning":"不做充分准备，临场发挥","example":"I wouldn't wing it for a job interview."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a rough outline / a rough plan","meaning":"大致框架；粗略计划","example":"I just need a rough plan, not a detailed itinerary."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a minute-by-minute schedule","meaning":"精确到每分钟的安排","example":"I don't need a minute-by-minute schedule."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"last-minute plans / at the last minute","meaning":"临时安排／最后关头","example":"I'm not a fan of last-minute plans."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"high-stakes","meaning":"事关重大的；风险较高的","example":"I prepare carefully for high-stakes situations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"know your limits","meaning":"了解自身极限","example":"You have to know your own limits on a hike."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take someone's word for it","meaning":"因为某人这么说就相信","example":"I wouldn't just take his word for it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"more nuanced than ...","meaning":"比……更有细微差别","example":"My approach to planning is more nuanced than that."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"micromanage / micromanagement","meaning":"事无巨细地控制","example":"I like planning, but not micromanagement."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a general plan but flexible details","meaning":"有总体安排，细节灵活","example":"I prefer a general plan with some flexibility."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a brutal uphill climb","meaning":"一段非常折磨人的上坡","example":"The first two kilometres were a brutal uphill climb."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the trail levels out","meaning":"山路变平缓","example":"After the steep section, the trail levels out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I've come this far, so I might as well ...","meaning":"都已经走到这了，索性……","example":"I've come this far, so I might as well finish."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I didn't come all this way just to ...","meaning":"大老远来这儿可不是为了……","example":"I didn't come all this way just to turn back."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"worth the effort / worth it","meaning":"值得付出／值得","example":"The climb was exhausting, but it was worth it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"breathtaking views","meaning":"美得令人屏息的风景","example":"The views from the ridge were breathtaking."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"settle in / settle into a rhythm","meaning":"渐渐适应／进入节奏","example":"It takes me a while to settle into a rhythm."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"go at your own pace","meaning":"按自己的节奏来","example":"I like hiking solo because I can go at my own pace."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel drawn to nature","meaning":"自然而然被大自然吸引","example":"Even people who don't hike may feel drawn to nature."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"let my mind wander","meaning":"任思绪自由飘荡","example":"On long walks, I just let my mind wander."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"switch off","meaning":"让脑子暂时从工作和烦恼中抽离","example":"Being outdoors helps me switch off."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get something off your chest","meaning":"把憋在心里的事说出来","example":"It's nice to get things off your chest."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"bottle things up","meaning":"把情绪压在心里","example":"You don't have to bottle everything up."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"vent (to someone)","meaning":"向某人倾诉、发牢骚","example":"Sometimes I just need to vent to a friend."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"bring people closer","meaning":"让彼此关系更近","example":"Going through a tough experience can bring people closer."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a low-pressure opener","meaning":"没有压力的开场白","example":"“Beautiful day, isn't it?” is a low-pressure opener."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"keep to myself","meaning":"喜欢自己待着，不太主动社交","example":"I usually keep to myself when I travel."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"drain someone's energy","meaning":"消耗某人精力","example":"Big social events can drain my energy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be open to ...","meaning":"对……持开放态度","example":"I enjoy solo hiking, but I'm open to a chat."},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'm not the kind of person who needs every little detail planned out.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I don't really like being invited somewhere at the last minute.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Especially if it's something that takes up a lot of time.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A hike can take a whole day, or even several days.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'd read up on the trail and check where it's safe to stay overnight.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"He'd need to know my fitness level and how active I normally am.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"They can't guarantee it'll be safe for me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The thought of hiking at 4,500 metres put a damper on my excitement.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A lot of things can go wrong at high altitude.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The first two kilometres are a brutal uphill climb.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Every hike I've done has felt worth it in the end.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The more trails you hike, the more similar the scenery can start to feel.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I've seen just about every kind of landscape.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Travel halfway around the world.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"People spend too much time indoors, especially in offices and cities.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can just let my mind wander without any interruptions.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"You can complain freely without being judged.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"You don't have to bottle everything up or deal with those feelings on your own.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"When you both vent about how exhausting the hike is, it can bring you closer.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'm an introvert, and there usually aren't many people on those trails.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'd go up to them and say hi.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Hey, how's it going? Beautiful view, isn't it?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I'm an INTJ, and I definitely prefer having some kind of plan. I don't need a minute-by-minute schedule, but I'm not a big fan of last-minute decisions either, especially when something takes up a whole day or more. If it's just a short, straightforward hike at low altitude, I'm happy to be flexible. But for a multi-day hike or anything at high altitude, I wouldn't just wing it. I'd read up on the route, check the weather, and make sure I know what I'm getting into.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"One thing I've noticed is that some hikes are toughest right at the beginning. I remember a trail where the first two kilometres were a brutal uphill climb. Once I'd got through that section, the path levelled out and the rest was much more straightforward. Even when I feel exhausted, I sometimes tell myself, “I've come this far, so I might as well keep going.” Most of the time, the views turn out to be breathtaking, and I feel it was worth the effort. Of course, I'd turn back if conditions got genuinely dangerous.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I love hiking for the scenery, but it's not just about the views. What I really enjoy is the sense of freedom. Sometimes I completely switch off and just take in what's around me. Other times, I let my mind wander. I might think about work, the stock market, or random things that have been bothering me, but I still feel relaxed. Out there, nobody's constantly interrupting me or handing me another task. I can think about whatever I want, at my own pace.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I'm quite introverted, so most of the time I'd rather hike on my own. I like being able to go at my own pace and enjoy the peace and quiet. But that doesn't mean I don't want to talk to anyone. If I run into another hiker, I'm happy to say hi, and sometimes I might strike up a conversation. Something simple like “Beautiful view, isn't it?” is enough. I like having the freedom to chat when I feel like it, without feeling obligated to socialize the whole time.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I made 200 this month.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I only made 200 this month.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Why do I have so much to do?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I've got a lot on my plate right now.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I've been swamped lately.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"clear up","meaning":"天气转晴；澄清（视语境）","example":"It looks like it'll clear up this afternoon."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cool / chilly / cold / freezing / bitterly cold","meaning":"凉快／冷飕飕／冷／冷得厉害／刺骨的冷","example":"It's chilly this morning, but not freezing."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"something came up","meaning":"临时有事；突然出了状况","example":"Sorry, something came up and I can't make it tonight."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"push something back","meaning":"把某项安排往后推","example":"Can we push our meeting back by an hour?"},{"kind":"phrase","front":"raise ethical concerns","meaning":"引发诚信/伦理上的担忧（略正式但常用）","example":"Making up experience on a CV raises ethical concerns."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make things up","meaning":"编造事实","example":"I don't want to make things up just to land a job."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"exaggerate my experience","meaning":"夸大工作经验","example":"I'd rather be honest than exaggerate my experience."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a red flag","meaning":"危险信号；令人警觉之处","example":"Being told to keep up a false story is a red flag."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"keep up an image / keep up appearances","meaning":"维持某种形象／做表面功夫","example":"I'd have to keep up an image that isn't really me."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"if it comes out / comes to light","meaning":"如果事情曝光；被发现","example":"If it comes out, it could have serious consequences."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"face consequences","meaning":"承担后果","example":"The agency could face consequences too."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take time off","meaning":"请假、休假","example":"I need to take time off for exams."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"spread out throughout the semester","meaning":"分散在整个学期","example":"My exams are spread out throughout the semester."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"commit to a full-time role","meaning":"承诺投入全职岗位","example":"I can't commit to a full-time role right now."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn down an offer / decline an offer","meaning":"拒绝工作机会（decline 较正式）","example":"I've decided to turn down the offer."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"walk away","meaning":"选择退出，不再继续","example":"Sometimes it's better to walk away."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"jeopardize something","meaning":"使某事面临风险","example":"I don't want to jeopardize my degree."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"at the end of the day","meaning":"说到底，归根结底","example":"At the end of the day, finishing my degree comes first."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"gross me out","meaning":"让我恶心、反胃","example":"Finding the toilet unflushed really grosses me out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"give someone the benefit of the doubt","meaning":"暂时往好处想，相信对方不是故意的（建议延伸）","example":"I gave him the benefit of the doubt at first."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my first sip / take a sip","meaning":"第一口（饮品）／抿一口","example":"The moment I took my first sip, I knew I hated it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"spit it out / spat it out","meaning":"把东西吐出来／过去式","example":"The coffee tasted awful, so I spat it out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put someone off something","meaning":"使某人对某物失去兴趣、产生反感","example":"The smell puts me off coffee."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the aftertaste","meaning":"余味，回味","example":"I can't stand the bitter aftertaste."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"gentle and comforting","meaning":"温和、让人舒服安心","example":"Tea feels gentler and more comforting to me."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"oats / oatmeal / peanut butter","meaning":"燕麦／燕麦粥／花生酱","example":"I usually have oats or toast with peanut butter."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the idea of working full-time puts me off","meaning":"“全职工作这个念头让我反感”","example":"It's not just one company; the idea of working full-time puts me off."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get enough in return","meaning":"获得足够回报","example":"People work long hours but don't always get enough in return."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"job security is shaky","meaning":"工作稳定性不可靠","example":"Even well-paid jobs can feel insecure when job security is shaky."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a decent salary / decent pay","meaning":"还不错的工资","example":"A decent salary doesn't necessarily mean a comfortable life."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be protective of one's time","meaning":"很珍惜、保护自己的时间","example":"Younger workers may be more protective of their free time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put food on the table","meaning":"养家糊口；满足基本生存需要","example":"In the past, many people worked simply to put food on the table."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel empty / unfulfilled","meaning":"精神空虚／缺乏成就或满足感","example":"You can have enough money and still feel unfulfilled."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"admission fee / admission ticket","meaning":"门票费用／入场票","example":"Some attractions charge a pretty steep admission fee."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make things worse / intensify","meaning":"加剧、使情况恶化（前者更口语）","example":"Social media can make that pressure worse."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the goalposts keep moving","meaning":"标准不断抬高，永远不够","example":"Every time people earn more, the goalposts seem to keep moving."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"barrier to entry","meaning":"入门门槛","example":"The cost of equipment is a barrier to entry for skiing."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have a mind of your own","meaning":"有自己的主见（建议延伸）","example":"You can be influenced by others and still have a mind of your own."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"travel burnout","meaning":"旅行疲劳、旅行倦怠","example":"I think I've got a bit of travel burnout."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"mentally drained / mentally exhausted","meaning":"精神疲惫","example":"After so many trips, I felt mentally drained."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"diminishing returns","meaning":"边际体验递减（生活、商业都能用）","example":"After seeing so many similar churches, there are diminishing returns."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"magnificent / grand","meaning":"宏伟壮观／富丽堂皇","example":"The cathedral was absolutely magnificent."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"intricate stone carvings","meaning":"精巧繁复的石雕","example":"I was amazed by the intricate stone carvings."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"underwhelming","meaning":"没预想中惊艳；让人失望","example":"The next church felt a bit underwhelming."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"raise the bar","meaning":"抬高标准或期待","example":"Seeing Rome's churches really raised the bar for me."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"blur together","meaning":"在记忆里逐渐混成一片","example":"After a while, all those old towns start to blur together."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stand out","meaning":"格外突出、令人印象深刻","example":"That little chapel actually stood out from the others."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"tick things off a list","meaning":"为打卡而打卡、逐项完成清单","example":"I don't want to spend every trip just ticking things off a list."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get the most out of something","meaning":"尽量获得最多收获","example":"I used to try to get the most out of every trip."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel like work","meaning":"感觉像是在工作／完成任务","example":"Planning a holiday shouldn't feel like work."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"wasn't particularly aware of it at the time","meaning":"当时没有特别清晰地意识到","example":"I wasn't particularly aware of the fatigue at the time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"much more noticeable now","meaning":"现在更加明显、能清楚感知","example":"That feeling is much more noticeable now."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"at the last minute / last-minute change","meaning":"最后一刻／临时变动","example":"A last-minute change is fine if you tell me right away."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"let someone know right away","meaning":"立即通知某人","example":"Just let me know right away if you can't make it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"on short notice","meaning":"提前通知时间很短","example":"I don't mind changes on short notice if there's a good reason."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"once in a while / occasionally","meaning":"偶尔","example":"I can understand being late once in a while."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"question the friendship","meaning":"质疑这段友谊是否值得维持","example":"It makes me question the friendship."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stay friends with someone","meaning":"继续和某人做朋友","example":"I'm not sure I want to stay friends with someone who's always late."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not worth the hassle","meaning":"不值得这样折腾","example":"Constantly rearranging plans isn't worth the hassle."},{"kind":"sentence","front":"If the forecast says it's going to pour, I'll stay home.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I like going hiking on a warm, sunny, breezy day.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'd cancel the plan and stay home.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It was an interview for a software testing engineer position.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A few things about the offer are bothering me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It raises some serious ethical concerns.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"There could be serious consequences if it comes to light.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It's tempting, but not tempting enough to give up my degree for.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It clashes with my exam schedule.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can't commit to a full-time position right now.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'd be happy to stay in touch about future opportunities.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I've already decided to turn down the offer.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I've run out of patience.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I kept giving him the benefit of the doubt.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The moment I took my first sip, I spat it out.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I had bread with peanut butter.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Even the smell of coffee puts me off.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Why are so many young people fed up with work?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"We're far more productive than ever before.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Just to put food on the table and avoid going hungry.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Feeling empty or unfulfilled.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Social media makes that pressure even worse.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"If you want to go skiing...","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I just don't have the energy to plan another trip.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Other churches might feel underwhelming by comparison.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I wasn't particularly aware of that feeling at the time.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"After a while, they all start to blur together.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Sometimes something unexpected comes up at the last minute.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can understand it if it happens once in a while.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I'd start wondering whether I even want to stay friends.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I had an interview for a software testing position, and the salary was pretty tempting. But a couple of things bothered me. For one thing, they wanted me to make up experience on my CV and keep up that story once I started working. That's a huge red flag for me. On top of that, the full-time schedule clashes with my exams. At the end of the day, it's just not worth jeopardizing my degree. So I've decided to turn the offer down. I'd rather be upfront about it and stay in touch in case something more suitable comes up later.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"Thanks, but coffee really isn't for me. I gave it a try once in Finland, and the moment I took my first sip, I wanted to spit it out. I don't know if it's the bitterness, the smell, or the aftertaste, but the whole thing puts me off. Tea is different, though. Even when it's bitter, I find it gentler and more comforting. So if you've got tea, I'd happily have that instead.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I don't think young people necessarily hate doing anything productive. A lot of us just feel that full-time jobs take up too much of our lives, and we don't always get enough in return. We're more productive than ever, yet the goalposts keep moving. Once you can put food on the table, you start wanting experiences, hobbies, and more freedom. And social media can make that pressure even worse. So there's this contradiction: you need money to enjoy your free time, but you have to give up so much of that time to earn it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I traveled to a lot of places in a short period, and I think I got a bit burned out. I still love traveling, but planning another trip sometimes feels like work. I've seen so many magnificent churches and intricate stone carvings in Italy that smaller churches can feel a little underwhelming by comparison. It's not that they're bad. It's just that the bar has been raised. After a while, old towns and city halls start to blur together. Looking back, I wasn't particularly aware of how tired I was at the time, but it's much more noticeable now. I'd rather slow down and choose a few places that genuinely interest me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cook most of my meals myself","meaning":"大部分饭自己做","example":"I cook most of my meals myself, whether they’re quick and easy or more time-consuming."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"add ingredients in the right order","meaning":"按正确顺序下食材","example":"With one pot, I have to add the ingredients in the right order."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get the timing right","meaning":"掌握烹饪时机","example":"It’s tricky to get the timing right when everything goes into one pot."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"save the quick-cooking ingredients for last","meaning":"易熟食材最后放","example":"I cook the vegetables that take longer first and save the spinach for last."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn mushy","meaning":"煮得软烂、糊软","example":"If you add spinach too early, it can turn mushy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"follow a recipe / improvise","meaning":"按菜谱做／临场发挥","example":"Sometimes I follow a recipe, but often I just improvise."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"time-consuming","meaning":"耗时的","example":"Cooking a full meal can be surprisingly time-consuming."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a trade-off","meaning":"权衡，有得有失","example":"There’s a trade-off between saving money and saving time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pay a little extra for convenience","meaning":"多付一点钱换方便","example":"Sometimes I’m happy to pay a little extra for convenience."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a shared / communal kitchen","meaning":"公用厨房","example":"I don’t enjoy using the shared kitchen in my dorm."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"unhygienic","meaning":"不卫生的","example":"The communal kitchen often feels unhygienic to me."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"limit my options","meaning":"限制选择","example":"Having only an electric pot really limits my options."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cookware / kitchenware / kitchen utensils","meaning":"锅具／厨房用品总称／厨用工具","example":"Cleaning my cookware and kitchen utensils afterward takes time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stove / stovetop","meaning":"炉灶／炉灶表面","example":"I don’t have a stove or an oven in my dorm room."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"clean up / the cleanup","meaning":"清理（动词）／收拾清洗（名词）","example":"The cleanup sometimes takes longer than the cooking."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"do the math","meaning":"算过账、核算成本","example":"I did the math, and eating out occasionally is affordable for me."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a source of protein","meaning":"蛋白质来源","example":"Meat is one source of protein, but it isn’t the only one."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a cold draft (UK: draught)","meaning":"从窗户透进来的冷风","example":"When I open the window in winter, a cold draft comes in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a window seal / a gap in the frame","meaning":"窗户密封条／窗框缝隙","example":"A gap in the window frame can let cold air in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"noise coming through thin walls","meaning":"穿过薄墙传来的噪音","example":"I can hear noise coming through the thin walls."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"heavy footsteps / chair scrapes","meaning":"沉重脚步声／椅子拖刮声","example":"My neighbor’s heavy footsteps and chair scrapes are distracting."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a low-frequency thump","meaning":"低频咚咚震动声","example":"The most annoying sound is a low-frequency thump."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"mask the noise","meaning":"用另一种声音掩盖噪音","example":"I want some background noise that can mask the thumping."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a steady background sound","meaning":"持续稳定的背景声音","example":"A steady background sound can be less distracting than sudden thumps."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"mentally exhausted / mentally drained","meaning":"精神疲惫的／心力交瘁的","example":"After practicing English for an hour, I felt mentally drained."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make progress / feel frustrated","meaning":"取得进步／感到挫败","example":"I can tell I’m making progress, but I still get frustrated sometimes."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"follow a lecture","meaning":"听懂、跟上讲座或授课","example":"I couldn’t really follow what the lecturer was saying."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pay attention in class","meaning":"上课认真听讲","example":"Very few students were actually paying attention in class."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"show up for class","meaning":"出席课程","example":"A lot of students didn’t even show up for class."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a lab session / lab class","meaning":"实验课","example":"In the lab session, we mainly reviewed mistakes in the materials."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"go over mistakes","meaning":"逐一检查、讲解错误","example":"The lecturer went over the mistakes and explained how to fix them."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"balance studying and working","meaning":"平衡学习和工作","example":"I’m constantly trying to balance studying and working."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"weigh my options","meaning":"权衡各种选项","example":"I have to weigh my options whenever work overlaps with class."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"opportunity cost","meaning":"机会成本：选择一项而放弃的次优收益","example":"If I attend class, the opportunity cost is the money I could have earned."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my time would be better spent elsewhere","meaning":"我的时间花在别处可能更值得","example":"I can’t help but wonder if my time would be better spent elsewhere."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get something out of something","meaning":"从某事中获得价值／收获","example":"It’s frustrating when I don’t feel I’m getting much out of a class."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put in the effort / get little in return","meaning":"付出努力／回报很少","example":"I’m willing to put in the effort, but sometimes I get little in return."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get my point across","meaning":"把意思表达清楚","example":"I can usually get my point across, even if my grammar isn’t perfect."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have a good command of English","meaning":"很好地掌握英语","example":"I want to have a better command of everyday English."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"master every word","meaning":"掌握每一个词","example":"I don’t need to master every word to communicate effectively."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"major grammatical mistakes","meaning":"严重的语法错误","example":"I want to avoid major grammatical mistakes, but minor ones are fine."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the flow of a conversation","meaning":"对话的流畅度／节奏","example":"Too much hesitation can interrupt the flow of a conversation."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"speak smoothly and naturally","meaning":"流畅自然地说话","example":"I want to express myself more smoothly and naturally."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"go beyond small talk","meaning":"不止停留在寒暄","example":"I want to go beyond small talk with native speakers."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have an in-depth conversation","meaning":"进行深入交流","example":"I’d like to have more in-depth conversations about social issues."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"dig a little deeper","meaning":"进一步深入讨论","example":"We can dig a little deeper without turning it into a lecture."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"only scratch the surface","meaning":"仅触及表面","example":"Today we only scratched the surface of the subject."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take a more academic approach","meaning":"从更偏学术的角度入手","example":"Sometimes I want to take a slightly more academic approach."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the underlying mechanisms","meaning":"背后的机制","example":"I’m interested in the psychological mechanisms underlying our choices."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"refer to a study / cite an article","meaning":"提及研究／引用论文","example":"In casual conversation, we can refer to a study without formally citing it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"draw on research","meaning":"借助研究结果支撑观点","example":"You can draw on research without using academic language all the time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"choose every word with absolute precision","meaning":"字斟句酌、准确选词","example":"I don’t need to choose every word with absolute precision."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"social comparison","meaning":"社会比较","example":"Social comparison existed long before social media."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"in relative rather than absolute terms","meaning":"用相对而非绝对标准衡量","example":"We often judge our success in relative rather than absolute terms."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the highlight reel of someone’s life","meaning":"他人生活的高光剪辑","example":"Social media mostly shows the highlight reels of other people’s lives."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"hedonic adaptation","meaning":"享乐适应：逐渐习惯生活改善","example":"Hedonic adaptation may help explain why new comforts stop feeling special."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"act as an amplifier / amplify","meaning":"成为放大器／放大","example":"Social media can act as an amplifier of social comparison."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"set unrealistic expectations","meaning":"制造不切实际的期待","example":"Constant exposure to luxury lifestyles can set unrealistic expectations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fuel envy and dissatisfaction","meaning":"加剧羡慕与不满","example":"Unfair comparisons can fuel envy and dissatisfaction."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"measure your self-worth by ...","meaning":"用……衡量自我价值","example":"It’s exhausting to measure your self-worth by other people’s achievements."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the rat race / be caught up in the rat race","meaning":"激烈的竞争生活／陷入内卷竞争","example":"Some people feel caught up in the rat race from an early age."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"outperform others","meaning":"表现超过别人","example":"Competition becomes stressful when you feel you must always outperform others."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get ahead","meaning":"出人头地、取得优势","example":"Everyone seems to be trying to get ahead."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"wear someone down","meaning":"使人长期疲惫、消磨意志","example":"Constant comparison can wear people down over time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"attach too much importance to ...","meaning":"过度看重……","example":"Why do we attach so much importance to being better off than others?"},{"kind":"phrase","front":"compare ourselves with others","meaning":"将自己与他人比较","example":"We’ve been comparing ourselves with others since we were very young."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"exceptional lifestyles as the norm","meaning":"把极少数人的优越生活当作常态","example":"The problem starts when we treat exceptional lifestyles as the norm."},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I occasionally go out to restaurants.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"You have to add the ingredients in the right order.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"How could these two issues possibly be connected?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’ve been getting a little lazy lately.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Very few students were actually paying attention in class.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Students were on their phones.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I sometimes make grammatical mistakes.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m mainly focused on everyday communication.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"We didn’t go into much depth.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"We’ve been comparing ourselves with others since we were young.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I cook most of my meals myself, but I've started eating out once or twice a week. I did the math, and it doesn't cost me that much. The biggest issue is that I live in a dorm and only have an electric pot in my room. Without a proper stove, my options are limited. Even making noodles takes planning because I have to add the ingredients in the right order. Sometimes I wonder whether spending so much time cooking is really worth the hassle.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"My neighbor's heavy footsteps and chair scrapes come through the thin walls as low-frequency thumps. I open my window to let in background noise that masks them, but in winter a cold draft comes in too.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"This morning, I practiced English for about an hour before going to class. I could tell I was making progress, but I still felt mentally exhausted. The lectures were even more frustrating because I couldn't always follow what the lecturer was saying. At the same time, I noticed that the rates on my delivery app had gone up. That made me think about the opportunity cost of staying in class. I know education matters, but I can't help wondering whether my time would sometimes be better spent elsewhere.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"My main goal isn't to become a translator or use complicated academic language. I want to have a good command of everyday English so I can communicate naturally with people from different backgrounds. I can usually get my point across, but sometimes I struggle to find the right words. I don't mind making minor grammatical mistakes as long as they don't cause misunderstandings. What matters most to me is being able to go beyond small talk and have more in-depth conversations.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I think social comparison is part of human nature. Even before social media, people compared themselves with neighbors, classmates, and colleagues. Social media acts as an amplifier: now we can see the lifestyles of extremely wealthy people thousands of miles away. That can set unrealistic expectations and fuel envy and dissatisfaction. In my experience growing up in China, competition started early, with comparisons of grades and achievements. The goalposts kept moving, and it sometimes felt like the rat race would never end. I don't think competition is always harmful, but constantly measuring your self-worth against other people can be mentally exhausting.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"shake out your clothes","meaning":"把衣服抖开、甩一甩","example":"Give your clothes a good shake before hanging them up."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"hang them up to dry","meaning":"挂起来晾干","example":"Shake them out before you hang them up to dry."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get all wrinkled","meaning":"变得皱巴巴","example":"They’ll get all wrinkled if you leave them in a pile."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"crumpled / wrinkled","meaning":"揉成一团、皱成一团 / 表面起褶皱","example":"The shirt was crumpled in my bag and came out wrinkled."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"walk towards each other","meaning":"相向而行；迎面走来","example":"We were walking towards each other along the pavement."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"approach each other","meaning":"逐渐靠近彼此","example":"Two people were approaching each other from opposite directions."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"walk past each other","meaning":"相向走过、擦肩而过","example":"We walked past each other without saying a word."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"almost bump into each other","meaning":"差点迎面撞上","example":"We almost bumped into each other at the doorway."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"leverage ...","meaning":"充分利用（常见于商业语境）","example":"Investors sometimes leverage their experience to spot opportunities."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fall into a routine / be in a routine","meaning":"形成固定作息、进入规律","example":"I’ve fallen into a routine: breakfast, campus, study, repeat."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my days blur together","meaning":"每天都差不多，日子混在一起","example":"I do similar things every day, so my days blur together."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a repetitive routine","meaning":"重复性的日常","example":"My routine is repetitive, but I don’t mind it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not a morning person / an early bird","meaning":"不习惯早起的人 / 早起型的人","example":"I’m not a morning person, even though I get up early."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a night owl","meaning":"夜猫子、晚间精力旺盛的人","example":"I’m definitely a night owl; I think more clearly at night."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel mentally alert","meaning":"头脑清醒、精神敏锐","example":"I feel much more mentally alert after sunset."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my brain kicks into gear","meaning":"大脑开始进入状态","example":"It takes a while for my brain to kick into gear."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"get a second wind","meaning":"突然恢复精力","example":"I often get a second wind late at night."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel groggy","meaning":"刚睡醒昏沉","example":"I feel groggy for quite a while after waking up."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take time to get going","meaning":"需要时间进入状态","example":"It takes me longer than average to get going in the morning."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"warm up mentally","meaning":"让头脑慢慢进入状态","example":"I need time to warm up mentally before doing difficult work."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"carve out some quiet time","meaning":"挤出、专门留出安静时间","example":"I’ve carved out a few hours to study without distractions."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a small price to pay for ...","meaning":"为了……值得付出的一点代价","example":"A ten-minute walk is a small price to pay for a quiet day."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my mood goes downhill","meaning":"心情变差、一路下滑","example":"When the thumping starts, my mood goes downhill."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"heavy thuds / thumping","meaning":"沉重的咚咚声、撞击声","example":"Heavy thuds from next door make it hard to concentrate."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"crack the window open","meaning":"把窗户开一条缝","example":"I cracked the window open to let some air in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"leave the window slightly open","meaning":"窗户留一条小缝","example":"I leave the window slightly open even when it’s cold."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"let some fresh air in","meaning":"让新鲜空气进来","example":"A little fresh air helps me stay awake."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cut right through my jacket","meaning":"冷风穿透衣服、吹得透心凉","example":"The wind at eight in the morning cut right through my jacket."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"wear two mid-layers","meaning":"穿两层中间保暖层","example":"I had to wear two mid-layers to stay warm."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"soak up some sunshine","meaning":"晒晒太阳、享受阳光","example":"I’m just sitting by the window, soaking up some sunshine."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the radiator / the heating is on","meaning":"暖气片 / 暖气开着","example":"The heating is on, so the room gets warm quickly."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn the heating up / down","meaning":"把暖气调高 / 调低","example":"They turn the heating up when temperatures drop."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the room gets stuffy","meaning":"房间变得闷、不通风","example":"If the windows stay shut, the room gets stuffy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel drowsy","meaning":"昏昏欲睡","example":"An overheated room makes me feel drowsy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"perk me up","meaning":"使我精神一振","example":"A little cool air perks me up."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stay alert / clear-headed","meaning":"保持清醒 / 头脑清楚","example":"Fresh air helps me stay alert and clear-headed."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the Wi-Fi keeps dropping out","meaning":"无线网络总是断连","example":"The university Wi-Fi keeps dropping out in the middle of calls."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the connection cuts in and out","meaning":"网络连接时断时续","example":"The connection keeps cutting in and out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the Wi-Fi is unreliable / laggy","meaning":"无线网络不稳定 / 延迟很高","example":"It’s frustrating that the campus Wi-Fi is so unreliable."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a contradiction between A and B","meaning":"A 和 B 之间存在矛盾","example":"There can be a contradiction between efficiency and fairness."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a trade-off between A and B","meaning":"A 和 B 之间需要权衡","example":"There’s often a trade-off between efficiency and fairness."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"sound contradictory / paradoxical","meaning":"听起来矛盾 / 悖论式的","example":"It sounds paradoxical, but a small hassle can save time later."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"tension between two goals","meaning":"两个目标之间的张力与冲突","example":"There’s tension between maximizing efficiency and ensuring fairness."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"push in different directions","meaning":"朝不同方向拉扯、彼此冲突","example":"The two goals sometimes push in different directions."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"sacrifice some fairness for efficiency","meaning":"为提高效率牺牲一部分公平","example":"Improving efficiency can sometimes mean sacrificing some fairness."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a turning point / a contrast","meaning":"转折点 / 对照转折关系","example":"Use “but” when the second clause introduces a genuine contrast."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take a nosedive","meaning":"突然大跌、断崖式下跌","example":"The market took a nosedive over a short period."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pull back / a pullback","meaning":"回撤、相对温和的调整","example":"A pullback sounds less dramatic than a plunge."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"weather the downturn","meaning":"挺过市场下行期","example":"My portfolio has weathered the downturn fairly well."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take a hit / hold up well","meaning":"受到冲击 / 顶住压力","example":"The market took a hit, but my portfolio held up well."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"outperform the market / an index","meaning":"跑赢市场 / 指数","example":"My portfolio has outperformed the Chinese market over that period."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"beat the market","meaning":"跑赢大盘（更口语）","example":"I’ve beaten the market so far this year."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"an investment portfolio / holdings","meaning":"投资组合 / 持仓","example":"A large part of my portfolio consists of U.S. holdings."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a niche interest","meaning":"小众兴趣","example":"Stock investing is still a niche interest in my social circle."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"opposing views / a counterargument","meaning":"相反观点 / 反驳论据","example":"I’m happy to read opposing views if they’re well reasoned."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"back up a claim with evidence","meaning":"用证据支持观点","example":"People should back up their claims with reasoning, not emotion."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"insider information / inside information","meaning":"内幕信息","example":"Most casual conversations don’t provide genuine inside information."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"already priced in","meaning":"已经反映在价格里","example":"That information might already be priced in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel self-conscious","meaning":"在意他人眼光而局促不安","example":"I sometimes feel self-conscious around strangers."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel neutral about ...","meaning":"对……既不紧张也不兴奋","example":"Sometimes I feel neutral about talking to classmates."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"socialize / be sociable","meaning":"参加社交、与人交往 / 善于交际","example":"I can socialize when I need to; I just don’t always want to."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"build a social network / network with people","meaning":"建立人际关系 / 社交拓展人脉","example":"Being introverted doesn’t mean I can’t network with people."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"social etiquette","meaning":"社交礼仪","example":"I usually follow social etiquette, even when I feel uncomfortable."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel obligated to stay","meaning":"觉得有义务留下","example":"I sometimes feel obligated to stay until the party ends."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"leave early / leave abruptly","meaning":"提前离开 / 突然离场","example":"I’d feel awkward leaving early while everyone else stayed."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"show up / make it to the event","meaning":"到场 / 赶得上活动","example":"I’m not sure I can make it to the meeting."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel drained / drain my energy","meaning":"感到精疲力尽 / 耗尽我的精力","example":"Long social gatherings can drain my energy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"enjoy my own company","meaning":"享受独处","example":"I enjoy my own company, reading or playing games."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be torn between A and B","meaning":"在 A 和 B 之间纠结","example":"I’m torn between staying home and going to a gathering."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’m torn between A and B","meaning":"在两个选择之间纠结","example":"I’m torn between cooking at home and getting KFC."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be on the fence about ...","meaning":"对……犹豫未决","example":"I’m still on the fence about ordering takeout."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"dry out","meaning":"失去水分，逐渐干掉","example":"The vegetables will dry out if I leave them too long."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’m not entirely sure what was in it","meaning":"我不太确定里面是什么","example":"I’m not entirely sure what was in the second burger."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"come with a sweet sauce","meaning":"配有甜酱","example":"One of the burgers came with a sweet sauce."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not really to my taste","meaning":"不太合我的口味","example":"That sauce wasn’t really to my taste."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"too sweet for my liking","meaning":"对我而言太甜了","example":"The sauce was a bit too sweet for my liking."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"savory / savoury","meaning":"咸鲜口的（美/英拼写）","example":"I like both sweet and savory food, just not that combination."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a large order of fries","meaning":"一大份薯条","example":"I had two chicken burgers and a large order of fries."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"plain broccoli","meaning":"不加调味的西兰花","example":"I usually eat plain broccoli to keep things simple."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"minced garlic / dice the garlic","meaning":"蒜末 / 把蒜切丁","example":"People often add minced garlic to vegetables."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cook through / cook quickly","meaning":"熟透 / 熟得快","example":"Different ingredients take different amounts of time to cook through."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the easiest / most effortless part","meaning":"最容易 / 最不费力的部分","example":"Boiling vegetables is the most effortless part of cooking."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the clean-up is easy","meaning":"收拾清洗很简单","example":"With one pot, the clean-up is easy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"purchasing power","meaning":"购买力","example":"Groceries cost less back home, so I’d have more purchasing power."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my money goes further","meaning":"同样的钱更经花","example":"My money would go a lot further in China."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not much of a shopper","meaning":"不太爱购物的人","example":"I’m not much of a shopper, so I don’t miss shopping malls."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not particularly materialistic","meaning":"物质欲望不强","example":"I’m not particularly materialistic, and I enjoy simple hobbies."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"my quality of life has taken a hit","meaning":"生活质量受到了影响","example":"My day-to-day quality of life has taken a hit in the dorm."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"day-to-day comfort / convenience","meaning":"日常舒适度 / 便利性","example":"I’ve given up some day-to-day comfort by moving abroad."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a trade-off / give up A in exchange for B","meaning":"取舍 / 放弃 A 换取 B","example":"I’ve traded some convenience for more opportunities abroad."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"broaden my horizons","meaning":"开阔眼界","example":"Living in Europe has helped me broaden my horizons."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"keep my options open","meaning":"给未来保留选择空间","example":"I want to keep my options open for the future."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a concrete benefit","meaning":"实实在在的好处","example":"Traveling around Europe is one concrete benefit of living here."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a round-trip ticket / airfare alone","meaning":"往返机票 / 光是机票","example":"The round-trip airfare alone could cost five hundred euros."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"worth the sacrifice","meaning":"值得为之牺牲","example":"Whether the experience is worth the sacrifice is a separate question."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"historical and cultural attractions / sites","meaning":"历史与人文景点","example":"I’m not especially interested in historical and cultural sites."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"ancient ruins / historical remains","meaning":"古代遗迹 / 历史遗存","example":"Many museums display objects and remains from earlier periods."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the Middle Ages / medieval history","meaning":"中世纪 / 中世纪历史","example":"I don’t always feel engaged by medieval history."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be famous for its history","meaning":"以其悠久历史著称","example":"Some cities are famous for their history."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have historical significance","meaning":"具有历史意义","example":"I know those places have historical significance."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a must-see attraction","meaning":"必看、必去景点","example":"I sometimes feel pressure to visit every must-see attraction."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a sense of duty / responsibility","meaning":"责任感、使命感","example":"It feels like a responsibility rather than genuine excitement."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"go out of obligation, not interest","meaning":"出于义务而非兴趣去做","example":"Sometimes I visit museums out of obligation, not interest."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"feel uncomfortable skipping it","meaning":"跳过会觉得不踏实","example":"I’d feel uncomfortable skipping an important historical site."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"natural scenery / scenic landscapes","meaning":"自然风景 / 风景优美的景观","example":"Natural scenery appeals to me far more than old buildings."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"snow-capped mountains / blue seas","meaning":"雪山 / 蔚蓝的海","example":"I get excited by snow-capped mountains and blue seas."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"hiking trails / coastal landscapes","meaning":"徒步路线 / 海岸景观","example":"I love hiking trails and coastal landscapes."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"lift my mood / turn my mood around","meaning":"改善心情、使心情好转","example":"A beautiful landscape can lift my mood immediately."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"come alive","meaning":"一下子精神起来、变得活跃","example":"I seem to come alive when I reach a scenic viewpoint."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"rather than a “want,” it feels like a “should”","meaning":"不是想去，而是觉得应该去","example":"Visiting some museums feels more like a “should” than a “want.”"},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Give your clothes a good shake, or they’ll get all wrinkled.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Two people are walking towards each other.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I eat basically the same breakfast and go to the same building every day.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m not a morning person.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I need somewhere quiet where nobody will interrupt me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It’s a bit of a hassle.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A little hassle now makes the rest of the day easier.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"This draft doesn’t make me feel cold.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"They turn the heating on in October.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"There’s often a trade-off between efficiency and fairness.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"How can I use “but” to show a contrast?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"My portfolio has outperformed the index.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"My portfolio outperformed the index over that period.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Stock investing is still a niche interest in my social circle.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The market may not care about that information.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It may already be priced in.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Sometimes people think I’m shy.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can socialize when I need to.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m more into spending time alone.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can’t promise I’ll be there.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m not sure I can make it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m torn between two options.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m torn between cooking at home and getting KFC.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"KFC is running a promotion today.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"KFC has a special offer.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It only costs nine euros.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I never used to notice these kinds of promotions.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some broccoli in my dorm room.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m not even sure what was in them.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A burger made with chicken.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The sweet sauce isn’t really to my taste.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Wait for the water to boil.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I have greater purchasing power.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"My quality of life has gone down.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’ve realized I’m not that interested in historical sites.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m interested in historical sites.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Natural scenery appeals to me much more.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I feel obligated to visit.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It feels like a responsibility.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"My days are pretty repetitive. I wake up around the same time, eat roughly the same breakfast, and head to the same academic building. I'm not really a morning person, so getting out of bed can be a struggle. But the dorm is noisy, and I need somewhere I can focus. Walking over to the building is a small price to pay for a whole day of peace. Once I'm there, I can study at my own pace without anyone interrupting me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I'm definitely a night owl. My brain seems to kick into gear later in the evening, and I can get a surprising amount done. In the morning, though, I feel groggy and need a while to get going. When the heating is on, the study room can get stuffy and make me drowsy. I usually crack the window open to let some fresh air in. Even if there's a slight draft, it perks me up and helps me stay alert.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"The Chinese stock market has plunged recently, but my portfolio has held up relatively well and outperformed the index over that period. I tend to keep my investment decisions to myself. Investing is still a niche interest in my social circle, and I don't find it useful to debate stocks with people who only repeat their feelings. I'm happy to read opposing views, but I want to see clear reasoning and evidence. Information that's already priced in doesn't really give me an edge.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"People sometimes assume I'm shy because I keep to myself. I can feel self-conscious in certain situations, but being introverted doesn't mean I can't socialize. It just means I enjoy my own company and need time to myself. When a conversation matters, I can take part. At parties, I usually follow social etiquette even if I'm not enjoying myself. That's partly why I prefer to decline invitations politely rather than leave early and feel awkward.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I was torn between cooking at home and getting KFC because there was a pretty good promotion on hot wings. The price was tempting, but I'd already had KFC the day before. I also had some broccoli in my room that was starting to turn yellow. So I was leaning towards cooking at home. I don't particularly enjoy plain broccoli, but boiling it is effortless: I just bring the water to a boil, add the broccoli, and wait a few minutes. The clean-up is easy too.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I'm not much of a shopper, so shopping malls and cinemas don't make much difference to me. Food and living conditions are another story. Back in China, my money would go further, and I'd have access to food that suits my taste. My quality of life has taken a hit in some day-to-day ways since I moved into a dorm. But living in Lithuania has also given me the opportunity to travel around Europe much more easily. I've visited around ten European countries, and the airfare alone would have made those trips more expensive from China. For now, I see it as a trade-off: less comfort in some areas, but more opportunities to broaden my horizons.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I've realized that I'm not as interested in historical and cultural sites as I once thought. I understand why ancient ruins, museums and medieval buildings matter to human civilization, and I sometimes feel obligated to visit them when I'm in a historic city. But that sense of duty isn't the same as genuine excitement. Natural scenery appeals to me much more. Snow-capped mountains, blue seas and hiking trails can lift my mood almost immediately. It's strange: I may feel tired after visiting several museums, but when I reach a beautiful natural landscape, I suddenly feel excited again. That reaction tells me a lot about what I really enjoy.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A is a small price to pay for B","meaning":"为了 B，A 是值得付出的小代价","example":"A ten-minute walk is a small price to pay for some peace."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"The idea of A is ... / A can be ...","meaning":"用抽象名词化方式表达评价","example":"The idea of leaving a famous site unseen makes me uncomfortable."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’m not really into + noun / -ing","meaning":"我不太喜欢……","example":"I’m not really into visiting museums."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"It’s not that ..., it’s just that ...","meaning":"不是说……而是……","example":"It’s not that I’m shy; it’s just that I enjoy being alone."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Even though + clause, main clause","meaning":"即使……仍然……","example":"Even though the market fell, my portfolio held up fairly well."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A appeals to me much more than B","meaning":"A 比 B 更吸引我","example":"Natural scenery appeals to me much more than historical sites."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I feel obligated to + verb","meaning":"感觉理应去做……","example":"I feel obligated to visit important historical sites."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I can’t help but + verb","meaning":"忍不住……","example":"I can’t help but wonder whether the experience is worth it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’ve realized that ...","meaning":"我逐渐意识到……","example":"I’ve realized that I prefer nature to museums."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A has taken a hit, but ...","meaning":"A 受到冲击，但……","example":"My daily comfort has taken a hit, but I’ve gained other opportunities."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Since + past point, present perfect","meaning":"自某时间点以来……","example":"Since I moved here, I’ve visited several European countries."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A has outperformed B over that period","meaning":"A 在那段期间跑赢 B","example":"My portfolio has outperformed the index over that period."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"If I’d ..., I would have ...","meaning":"与过去事实相反的假设","example":"If I’d stayed in China, traveling around Europe would have cost more."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"running late","meaning":"要迟到了","example":"I'm running late for class."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make it / barely make it","meaning":"赶到／勉强赶上","example":"We barely made it to the train on time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"go our separate ways","meaning":"各自离开","example":"After the meeting, we went our separate ways."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have the whole place to myself","meaning":"独占整个空间、几乎没人","example":"I had the whole study room to myself."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a sense of freedom","meaning":"自由感","example":"Walking alone gives me a sense of freedom."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"upbeat","meaning":"轻快、积极的","example":"She stayed upbeat despite the bad weather."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"come to mind","meaning":"浮现脑海","example":"Nothing comes to mind right now."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"keep someone up","meaning":"让某人睡不着","example":"The noise kept me up all night."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"soaked / wet / damp / dry","meaning":"湿透／湿／潮湿／干燥","example":"My jacket was soaked after the hike, but my socks stayed dry."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"leak / spill / drip / drain / splatter","meaning":"漏／洒／滴／排走／飞溅","example":"Water started dripping from the pipe."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"drag / bulky / get stuck / squeeze through","meaning":"拖／笨重／卡住／挤过去","example":"The bulky bag got stuck in the doorway."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stale / fresh","meaning":"不新鲜／新鲜","example":"The bread went stale overnight."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"firm / mushy","meaning":"紧实／软烂","example":"Cook the broccoli until it's tender but not mushy."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"ancient artifacts / ancient collections","meaning":"古代文物／古代藏品","example":"Museums put ancient artifacts on display."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"on display","meaning":"展出、陈列","example":"Is the original sculpture on display here?"},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a documentary","meaning":"纪录片","example":"I can learn a lot from books and documentaries."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"What can ... offer that ... can’t?","meaning":"……能提供什么……无法提供的？","example":"What can museums offer that books can’t?"},{"kind":"phrase","front":"gain knowledge / learn about history","meaning":"获得知识／了解历史","example":"If I only want to gain knowledge, I can read a book."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"see something in person","meaning":"亲眼看到","example":"Seeing a sculpture in person feels different from seeing a photo."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the scale, texture and atmosphere","meaning":"尺度、质感与氛围","example":"A photo doesn’t always capture the scale and texture."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"an original / a replica","meaning":"原作／复制品","example":"The statue in the square is a replica, not the original."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"craftsmanship / attention to detail","meaning":"工艺水平／对细节的关注","example":"I was blown away by the craftsmanship and attention to detail."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"intricate / sophisticated","meaning":"精细复杂的／精妙复杂的","example":"The sculpture looks incredibly intricate."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be blown away by","meaning":"被……深深震撼（口语）","example":"I was blown away by how detailed the sculpture was."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be astonished by / in awe of","meaning":"惊叹于／对……心生敬畏","example":"I was genuinely astonished by the work."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"exceptional / world-class","meaning":"出类拔萃的／世界级的","example":"I’d make time for a museum with something exceptional on display."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"struggle to see the point of","meaning":"难以理解做某事的意义","example":"I struggle to see the point of visiting an ordinary museum."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a lasting impression","meaning":"持久的印象","example":"The sculpture impressed me, but it didn’t leave a lasting emotional impact."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stay with someone","meaning":"在心中久久留存","example":"The feeling stays with me long after the hike."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"linger / a lingering feeling","meaning":"萦绕不散／余韵","example":"That sense of peace lingers for days."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"exhilarated","meaning":"畅快、兴奋不已","example":"I feel exhilarated when I reach an incredible viewpoint."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"invigorated","meaning":"精神振奋、充满活力","example":"I come back from the mountains feeling invigorated."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"uplifted / lift my spirits","meaning":"心情振奋／让我心情变好","example":"Those memories still lift my spirits."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"rejuvenated / refreshed","meaning":"焕然一新／恢复精神","example":"A few days outdoors leave me feeling refreshed."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fulfilled / a sense of fulfillment","meaning":"充实、满足／成就满足感","example":"Hiking gives me a real sense of fulfillment."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"inspired / eager to","meaning":"受到激励／迫不及待想……","example":"Remembering the trip makes me eager to hike again."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"look back on / think back to","meaning":"回想、回顾","example":"Even months later, I look back on those hikes fondly."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"long for / crave","meaning":"渴望、向往","example":"When city life gets stressful, I long for the mountains."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"clear my head / reset","meaning":"让头脑清醒／重新调整状态","example":"Being outdoors helps me clear my head."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"reconnect with nature","meaning":"重新亲近自然","example":"Sometimes I just want to reconnect with nature."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"subconsciously / deep down","meaning":"潜意识里／内心深处","example":"Deep down, I think we still feel connected to nature."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"consciously / without realizing it","meaning":"有意识地／不知不觉地","example":"We may feel that connection without realizing it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a fast-paced lifestyle","meaning":"快节奏的生活方式","example":"A fast-paced lifestyle can be mentally exhausting."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"things to get done / responsibilities to deal with","meaning":"要完成的事／需要处理的责任","example":"There’s always something to worry about and things to get done."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"escape into nature / get away from it all","meaning":"到自然中暂时逃离／远离日常纷扰","example":"On weekends I sometimes want to get away from it all."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the peace and quiet / the buzz of the city","meaning":"宁静／城市的热闹活力","example":"Some people enjoy the city’s buzz; others prefer the peace and quiet."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be accustomed to / take for granted","meaning":"习惯于／视为理所当然","example":"People can take familiar surroundings for granted."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be drawn to what is missing","meaning":"向往日常生活中缺少的东西","example":"We’re often drawn to whatever is missing from everyday life."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"it comes down to","meaning":"归根结底是……","example":"Maybe it comes down to what people feel is missing."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"raw data / unstructured data","meaning":"原始数据／非结构化数据","example":"Raw data isn’t always ready to analyze."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be scattered across","meaning":"分散在各处","example":"Useful information can be scattered across different websites."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"collect / scrape / process data","meaning":"收集／抓取／处理数据","example":"Code can help you scrape, clean and process data."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn data into useful insights","meaning":"把数据转化为有用见解","example":"I want to turn messy data into useful insights."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a skill gap / a missing piece","meaning":"技能短板／缺失的一环","example":"Programming was the missing piece in my previous work."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a systematic discipline","meaning":"系统性学科","example":"Software engineering is a systematic discipline, not just coding."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"identify and analyze requirements","meaning":"识别并分析需求","example":"Developers need to identify and analyze requirements."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"translate requirements into specifications","meaning":"将需求转化为软件规格说明","example":"You translate business requirements into technical specifications."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"design workflows / draw flowcharts","meaning":"设计工作流程／绘制流程图","example":"The team designs workflows before implementing the system."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"implement a solution / write the code","meaning":"实现解决方案／编写代码","example":"Finally, you implement the design in code."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I initially thought ... but later realized ...","meaning":"起初以为……后来意识到……","example":"I initially thought it was all about coding, but later realized there was much more to it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"an independent developer / a freelancer","meaning":"独立开发者／自由职业者","example":"I used to think I could work as an independent developer."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take on freelance projects / small gigs","meaning":"承接自由职业项目／小单子","example":"Some freelancers take on small website projects."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the going rate / charge for a project","meaning":"市场通常报价／项目收费","example":"The going rate for basic websites may be changing."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"rates have dropped sharply","meaning":"报价大幅下降","example":"I saw a video claiming that website-development rates have dropped sharply."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"boost productivity / get more done","meaning":"提升生产率／完成更多工作","example":"AI can help freelancers get more done in less time."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"disrupt the old paradigm","meaning":"打破旧有范式","example":"AI seems to be disrupting the old paradigm."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"rewrite the rules of the game","meaning":"改写游戏规则","example":"AI is rewriting the rules of the game."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn an industry upside down","meaning":"使行业发生天翻地覆的变化","example":"New technology can turn an industry upside down."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the essentials / necessities","meaning":"生活必需品","example":"I don’t shop much; I mainly buy essentials."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"shop online / in-store","meaning":"网购／到实体店购物","example":"I rarely shop online or in-store unless I need something."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"professional models / flattering angles","meaning":"专业模特／显好看的拍摄角度","example":"Brands use models and flattering camera angles."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"retouched / heavily edited photos","meaning":"修过图的／精修的照片","example":"Product photos can be heavily retouched."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"look amazing online / look different in person","meaning":"网上看着很棒／实物却不同","example":"The jacket looked amazing online but different in person."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the fit is off","meaning":"版型不合适","example":"The material feels okay, but the fit is off."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the material feels cheap","meaning":"材质摸起来廉价","example":"The material felt cheaper than I expected."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fall short of my expectations","meaning":"不符合我的期望","example":"The actual product fell short of my expectations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"live up to the pictures / expectations","meaning":"达到图片／期待的效果","example":"The shirt didn’t live up to the product photos."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"give a shop one more chance","meaning":"再给商家一次机会","example":"I might give the shop one more chance."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’m done with that shop","meaning":"我再也不去那家店了","example":"If they disappoint me twice, I’m done with that shop."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"leave a one-star review","meaning":"留一星评价","example":"If the product is genuinely awful, I might leave a one-star review."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"shrug it off / let it go","meaning":"一笑置之／不再计较","example":"Usually I just shrug it off and move on."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"not worth ruining my day over","meaning":"不值得为此坏了一天心情","example":"A disappointing purchase isn’t worth ruining my day over."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put me in a bad mood / get on my nerves","meaning":"使我心情变差／惹我心烦","example":"I won’t let one bad purchase put me in a bad mood."},{"kind":"sentence","front":"What can museums offer that books and documentaries can’t?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Seeing it in a film is completely different from standing in front of it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I was blown away by the David sculpture I saw in Florence.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The statue in the square was a replica.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"How could an artist create something so sophisticated centuries ago?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m not really into art.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Even months later, those memories still lift my spirits.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"We come from nature, so I think we’re still psychologically connected to it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"We aren’t always consciously aware of it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"When I’m hiking in the mountains ...","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The whole atmosphere stays with me.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It keeps drawing me back to that feeling.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"City life moves at a fast pace.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"There are so many things to get done every day.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Working on a farm or raising cattle and sheep.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"By contrast, they might be more drawn to city life.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The ability to handle large amounts of data.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some data is scattered across different websites.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"You need to collect or scrape that data.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Use code throughout the process, from collecting data to analyzing it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"AI can generate code to perform those tasks.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I hadn’t realized how systematic software engineering is.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Translate those requirements into detailed software specifications and designs.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I initially thought coding was the core of the degree.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Building small apps or simple websites.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Rates keep falling.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some freelancers might take on more projects thanks to AI.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"AI is disrupting the old paradigm and rewriting the rules of the game.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I mostly just buy essentials.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"They use professional models and heavily retouch the photos.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"They use flattering lighting and camera angles.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The clothes don’t look the same on you as they do on the model.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"These clothes / these pieces of clothing ...","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"If a shop sells me a low-quality product ...","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I won’t shop there again, and I may leave a one-star review.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It’s not worth wasting my time or ruining my mood over.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A product this bad shouldn’t be sold to customers.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"What can A offer that B can’t?","meaning":"比较两种选择独特价值。","example":"What can a museum offer that a documentary can’t?"},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Unless ..., I struggle to see the point of ...","meaning":"表达对特定活动价值的保留态度。","example":"Unless there’s something exceptional, I struggle to see the point of going."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Seeing A is different from experiencing B.","meaning":"区分媒介体验与现场体验。","example":"Seeing a mountain in a video is different from being there."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Even months later, I still ...","meaning":"长期效应。","example":"Even months later, those memories still lift my spirits."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I find myself + -ing","meaning":"不自觉地做某事。","example":"I find myself longing for the mountains when I’m stressed."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"from A to B","meaning":"描述完整流程。","example":"I want to automate the process from collecting data to analyzing it."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A is rewriting the rules of B.","meaning":"格局发生变化。","example":"AI is rewriting the rules of freelance software development."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"A looked ..., but when it arrived ...","meaning":"网购前后落差。","example":"The shirt looked great online, but when it arrived, the material felt cheap."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"It didn’t live up to ...","meaning":"现实低于预期。","example":"It didn’t live up to my expectations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"I’ll ... if ..., but otherwise I’ll ...","meaning":"带条件的日常取舍。","example":"I’ll complain if the quality is terrible, but otherwise I’ll let it go."},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I understand why people enjoy museums, and I know you can learn a lot from them. But if my main goal is to learn about history, I can usually get much of that information from books or documentaries. What I can’t get from a book is the feeling of standing in front of an original work and seeing its scale and craftsmanship in person. That’s why I’d definitely visit a museum with something truly exceptional on display. For an ordinary museum, though, I sometimes struggle to see what I’d get out of it.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"When I was in Florence, I saw a replica of Michelangelo’s David in the square. Even though it wasn’t the original, I was still blown away by its scale and attention to detail. It’s hard to imagine someone creating something so sophisticated more than five hundred years ago. But I’m not really an art enthusiast, so for me the experience was mostly a moment of amazement rather than something that changed my interests.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"For me, hiking is about more than beautiful scenery. It’s the whole atmosphere, especially that sense of freedom, that stays with me long after the trip. Even months later, thinking back to those moments still lifts my spirits and makes me eager to head out again. City life moves at such a fast pace that there’s always something to worry about or get done. Being out in nature gives me a chance to slow down and clear my head. Interestingly, someone who lives in a remote village might feel the opposite and be more drawn to city life. Maybe we’re often attracted to whatever is missing from our everyday lives.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I switched to software engineering because I wanted to combine my background in business analysis with programming. In my previous work, a lot of useful information was scattered across different websites, and it wasn’t always in a format I could analyze directly in Excel. I wanted to learn how to collect, clean and analyze that data more efficiently. But after starting the degree, I realized software engineering was much more than writing code. It also involved analyzing requirements, designing workflows and translating ideas into technical specifications. At the same time, AI is changing the way simple software projects are built, which makes me rethink what independent development might look like in the future.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I don’t buy much beyond the essentials. Sometimes clothes look amazing online because brands use professional models, flattering lighting and heavily edited photos. But when the item arrives, the fit might be off or the material might feel cheap. If the quality is truly unacceptable, I’d be annoyed and might leave a one-star review. Most of the time, though, I’d just shrug it off and avoid that shop in the future. A relatively small purchase isn’t worth wasting my time or ruining my mood over.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"buy the dip","meaning":"逢低买入","example":"Some investors I follow have started buying the dip."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"make a small purchase / make a small buy","meaning":"少量买入","example":"I made a small buy today, but it barely changed my allocation."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a token purchase / a token buy","meaning":"象征性买入、极小规模买入","example":"It was more of a token purchase than a meaningful addition."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a meaningful addition to my position","meaning":"对持仓有实质影响的加仓","example":"I don’t have enough spare cash to make a meaningful addition to my position."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"existing holdings","meaning":"现有持仓","example":"The purchase was tiny compared with my existing holdings."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"limited spare cash / limited dry powder","meaning":"可动用现金有限（dry powder 投资口语）","example":"With limited dry powder, I need to be selective."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"incremental purchases / buy in increments","meaning":"分批、小额地买入","example":"I’m building my position through incremental purchases."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"gradually build up a position","meaning":"逐步建立或增加仓位","example":"I’d rather gradually build up a position than rush in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"step up my purchases / accelerate my buying","meaning":"加快买入速度、增加买入量","example":"If prices fall further, I might step up my purchases."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"commit more capital","meaning":"投入更多资金","example":"I’m hesitant to commit more capital without a clear reason."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"broad-market index funds","meaning":"宽基指数基金","example":"I’ve mainly been buying broad-market index funds."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"stock picking / pick individual stocks","meaning":"主动选股","example":"I’m avoiding stock picking while the whole market is under pressure."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"capture broad-market returns","meaning":"获得宽基市场表现（不保证收益）","example":"An index fund lets me capture the benchmark’s returns without choosing individual winners."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"sell-off","meaning":"抛售、下跌行情","example":"The sell-off has continued for another week."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"drawdown / peak-to-trough decline","meaning":"回撤、从高点到低点的跌幅","example":"A large drawdown doesn’t automatically make an asset cheap."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pullback / correction / crash","meaning":"回调／较明显调整／崩盘（程度不同）","example":"This is more than a minor pullback, but a crash is a stronger word."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a full-blown crash","meaning":"全面、严重的崩盘","example":"I hope the sell-off doesn’t turn into a full-blown crash."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"oversold","meaning":"超卖（技术指标语境）","example":"The market may look oversold without being undervalued."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"undervalued / fairly valued / overvalued","meaning":"低估／估值合理／高估","example":"I wouldn’t call it undervalued, but it no longer looks especially expensive."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"historically attractive valuations","meaning":"历史上较有吸引力的估值","example":"I look for historically attractive valuations rather than just large price declines."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a convincing catalyst","meaning":"有说服力的催化因素","example":"I can’t identify a convincing catalyst for a sustained rebound."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"trigger a rebound / stage a rebound","meaning":"引发反弹／出现反弹","example":"Even a small improvement in sentiment could trigger a rebound."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a sustained recovery","meaning":"持续性复苏或回升","example":"A short-lived bounce isn’t the same as a sustained recovery."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"turn sentiment around","meaning":"扭转市场情绪","example":"Better earnings could help turn sentiment around."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"selling pressure eases / selling pressure is exhausted","meaning":"卖压缓解／卖压衰竭","example":"Markets can rebound when selling pressure starts to ease."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"bargain hunters step in","meaning":"逢低买入者进场","example":"Bargain hunters sometimes step in after a steep decline."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a bearish view / bearish voices","meaning":"看空观点／看空声音","example":"Even some bearish voices say valuations aren’t especially high."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"illustrate the severity of the sell-off","meaning":"说明抛售的严重程度","example":"I mentioned the drawdown to illustrate the severity of the sell-off, not to prove stocks are cheap."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"market-wide dislocation","meaning":"市场层面价格或定价出现明显偏离","example":"Long-term investors sometimes respond to rare market- wide dislocations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"be indifferent to valuations","meaning":"对估值不在意","example":"Long-term investing doesn’t mean being indifferent to valuations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"market timing / time the market","meaning":"择时／精准踩点入市","example":"Valuation-based decisions aren’t necessarily the same as trying to time every move."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"trim a position","meaning":"减持部分仓位","example":"An investor might trim a position when valuations become stretched."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"add aggressively","meaning":"较大力度地加仓","example":"Some investors add aggressively during major sell-offs."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"valuations look stretched","meaning":"估值偏高、被拉得过满","example":"I’d be cautious if valuations looked stretched."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fair value / intrinsic value","meaning":"合理价值／内在价值","example":"Price and intrinsic value can diverge."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"calling the bottom","meaning":"判断最低点","example":"Recognizing an attractive valuation isn’t the same as calling the bottom."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a good entry point","meaning":"合适的买入切入点","example":"A sharp decline may create a good entry point, but not automatically."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"have a track record","meaning":"有历史业绩记录、过往表现","example":"I follow investors who have a solid track record."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cautiously optimistic","meaning":"谨慎乐观","example":"I’m cautiously optimistic, but I’m keeping some cash in reserve."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"either scenario could play out","meaning":"两种情境都有可能发生","example":"Both scenarios are plausible, and either could play out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"adjust my assessment as new information comes in","meaning":"随着信息更新调整判断","example":"I adjust my assessment as new information comes in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"temporary volatility / structural change","meaning":"短期波动／结构性变化","example":"I try to distinguish temporary volatility from structural change."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"midterm elections","meaning":"美国国会中期选举","example":"Some investors expect uncertainty to ease after the midterm elections."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"retain control of Congress","meaning":"保持对国会的控制","example":"The market could react differently depending on which party retains control of Congress."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"political uncertainty weighs on sentiment","meaning":"政治不确定性压制市场情绪","example":"Political uncertainty may be weighing on investor sentiment."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"drag out a conflict","meaning":"拖延冲突","example":"One theory is that both sides have incentives to drag out the conflict."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"lose leverage / gain leverage","meaning":"失去／获得谈判筹码","example":"The theory assumes one side could lose leverage after the election."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"put political pressure on","meaning":"对……施加政治压力","example":"Higher energy prices could put political pressure on policymakers."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"take the gloves off","meaning":"不再留手、采取更强硬手段（口语比喻）","example":"Some commentators worry the administration might take the gloves off after the vote."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"exercise restraint / abandon restraint","meaning":"保持克制／不再克制","example":"An escalation scenario assumes the parties abandon restraint."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"destabilize / topple a government","meaning":"使政权不稳定／推翻政权（不同强度）","example":"A strike might destabilize a government; “topple” would mean actually bringing it down."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pave the way for","meaning":"为……铺平道路","example":"An easing of tensions might pave the way for a market recovery."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"spill over into","meaning":"外溢、传导至","example":"A U.S. rally could spill over into Chinese equities."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"global risk appetite","meaning":"全球风险偏好","example":"Falling yields can sometimes improve global risk appetite."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the 10-year Treasury yield","meaning":"美国 10 年期国债收益率","example":"A decline in the 10-year Treasury yield might support equity valuations."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"funds flow back into equities","meaning":"资金重新流入股票市场","example":"Some investors expect funds to flow back into equities."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"price in a risk / be priced in","meaning":"将风险计入资产价格／风险已被计价","example":"It’s hard to tell how much of that risk is already priced in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the market has already factored it in","meaning":"市场可能已经考虑了该因素","example":"Some investors think the market has already factored it in."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a risk isn’t fully priced in","meaning":"风险尚未被充分计价","example":"If the risk isn’t fully priced in, prices may react sharply."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a plausible scenario","meaning":"合理但未证实的情境","example":"I see this as a plausible scenario, not a firm prediction."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a speculative theory","meaning":"推测性的观点、理论","example":"It’s a speculative theory I came across online."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"play out","meaning":"（情境、局势）最终演变或发生","example":"We don’t know how the situation will play out."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"markets don’t always behave as expected","meaning":"市场未必按预期运行","example":"Markets don’t always behave as expected, even when an argument sounds convincing."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"fall further than expected","meaning":"跌幅超出预期","example":"Prices can fall further than even experienced investors expect."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"short-term horizon / long-term horizon","meaning":"短期／长期观察与投资期限","example":"Markets sometimes focus on a much shorter horizon during a crisis."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"heightened uncertainty","meaning":"加剧的不确定性","example":"Heightened uncertainty makes long-term predictions harder."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"revise our assumptions","meaning":"修正原有假设","example":"We have to revise our assumptions when the facts change."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a range of possible outcomes","meaning":"一系列可能结果","example":"I prefer thinking in terms of a range of possible outcomes."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"policy support / liquidity support","meaning":"政策支持／流动性支持","example":"Liquidity support could improve sentiment without guaranteeing a rally."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"underlying earnings power","meaning":"企业底层、可持续的盈利能力","example":"What matters most to me is a company’s underlying earnings power."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the ability to generate profits","meaning":"创造利润的能力","example":"I’d worry if its ability to generate profits was permanently damaged."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"earnings capacity","meaning":"盈利能力、利润创造能力","example":"A temporary setback doesn’t necessarily weaken long- term earnings capacity."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"structural deterioration","meaning":"结构性恶化","example":"Structural deterioration worries me more than a temporary slowdown."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"temporary headwinds","meaning":"短期不利因素","example":"Higher energy costs may create temporary headwinds."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"permanent impairment","meaning":"永久性损伤（价值、盈利能力等）","example":"A permanent impairment of earning power is a more serious concern."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"cyclical slowdown","meaning":"周期性放缓","example":"A cyclical slowdown can hurt profits without permanently destroying the business."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"profit margins get squeezed","meaning":"利润率受到挤压","example":"When input costs rise, manufacturers’ profit margins can get squeezed."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"input costs / operating costs","meaning":"投入成本／运营成本","example":"Higher input costs can reduce short-term profitability."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"pass costs on to customers","meaning":"把成本转嫁给消费者","example":"Some companies can pass higher costs on to customers."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"market share erosion / lose market share","meaning":"市场份额遭侵蚀／失去份额","example":"Losing market share for years could point to deeper problems."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"a temporary shock","meaning":"暂时性冲击","example":"An oil-price spike could be a temporary shock for some businesses."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"recover once pressure eases","meaning":"压力缓解后恢复","example":"Profits might recover once energy prices ease."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"industry-wide / economy-wide","meaning":"全行业的／整个经济层面的","example":"An industry-wide shock isn’t necessarily unique to a single company."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"macro-driven vs company-specific","meaning":"宏观因素驱动／公司自身因素","example":"I want to distinguish macro-driven weakness from company-specific damage."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"diversification / index exposure","meaning":"分散化／指数敞口","example":"Index exposure spreads company-specific risk across many holdings."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"the pace of the recovery","meaning":"复苏速度、节奏","example":"Some shocks change the pace of the recovery rather than the economy’s long-term potential."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"profitability has been impaired","meaning":"盈利能力已经受损","example":"I would slow my buying if long-term profitability had been impaired."},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’ve mainly been buying index funds.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It was more of a token purchase than a meaningful addition to my position.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I can only add to my position gradually, in small increments.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Which stocks would rebound faster than others?","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"At least capture broad-market returns.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Potential catalysts that could trigger a rebound.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"What concerns me is that... / I’m concerned that...","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It fell roughly 20% from its peak.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The market might go up.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some investors I follow have already started buying.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I have a fair amount of confidence in their judgment.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Markets don’t always move the way people expect.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I hope the sell-off doesn’t turn into a full-blown crash.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"People assume long-term investors don’t care about timing.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"When the market surges far beyond fair value.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Trim some positions.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Even some of the most bearish investors.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"This drawdown is extreme by historical standards.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some of the political uncertainty could ease after the election.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The 10-year Treasury yield could fall.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Money could flow back into equities.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Take the gloves off / abandon restraint.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Destabilize the Iranian government.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The conflict could escalate again.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Both views have their own logic.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Some investors have already factored in that possibility.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"I’m not sure how much of this risk is already priced in.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"The market might fall for a while before bouncing back.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It’s hard to predict events that far ahead.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Markets tend to price in near-term risks and adjust as circumstances change.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"A company’s underlying ability to generate profits.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Other factors may affect the timing of the recovery rather than long-term earnings power.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"They’ve lost some market share over the past few years.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Input costs are rising. / Costs are increasing.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Their costs could fall as oil prices ease.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"It may be a company-specific problem or a broader macroeconomic issue.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"sentence","front":"Many shocks affect the pace of the broader economy’s recovery.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"phrase","front":"Compared with / relative to ...","meaning":"与……相比，强调相对规模。","example":"Compared with my existing holdings, this was a tiny purchase."},{"kind":"phrase","front":"... might ... without necessarily ...","meaning":"避免过度推论。","example":"A temporary shock might hurt profits without necessarily impairing the business long term."},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I’ve mainly been buying broad-market index funds. Given how widespread the sell-off has been, I find it difficult to predict which individual stocks will rebound fastest. Rather than trying to pick the winners, I’d prefer to capture the performance of a broad benchmark. My latest purchase was tiny compared with my existing holdings—more of a token buy than a meaningful addition. I don’t have much spare cash, so I’m building my position in small increments. If valuations become even more attractive, I may step up my purchases.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"When I mention a 20% or 30% decline, I’m not using that number as proof that the market is cheap. I’m simply trying to illustrate the severity of the sell-off. I also look at other indicators, especially valuations and historical extremes. Even some bearish observers think certain parts of the market are no longer especially expensive. But that still doesn’t guarantee an immediate rebound. What worries me is that I can’t identify a convincing catalyst that would turn investor sentiment around and support a sustained recovery.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I think it’s misleading to assume that long-term investors don’t care about timing at all. There’s a difference between trying to predict every short-term market move and making occasional decisions based on valuation. If a broad market is under severe pressure and prices become attractive, a long-term investor may add to their holdings. On the other hand, if valuations become stretched, they may trim some positions. That doesn’t mean they can call the exact bottom or top. It simply means that long-term investing and valuation awareness can go hand in hand.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"I’ve come across two competing theories about what might happen after the U.S. midterm elections. One is that political uncertainty could ease, geopolitical tensions might cool down, and investor confidence could improve. That could pave the way for a rebound in U.S. equities, with some of the improvement in sentiment spilling over into Chinese stocks. The other theory is almost the opposite: once the vote is over, policymakers might feel less restrained, tensions could escalate, and markets might fall before recovering. I’m not presenting either theory as a fact. Both scenarios have some logic, but it’s difficult to know how much of the risk is already priced in.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"Some investors may have already factored a possible escalation into their expectations, but that doesn’t mean the risk is fully priced in across the market. A sudden development could still catch investors off guard. In a highly uncertain environment, long-range forecasts become less reliable, and markets often focus on near-term risks. Rather than assuming I can predict what will happen years from now, I prefer to think through several possible outcomes and revise my assessment as new information comes in.","meaning":"","example":""},{"kind":"paragraph","front":"What would really make me reconsider my buying plan is evidence of a lasting deterioration in companies’ underlying earnings power. Higher oil prices or a geopolitical shock may squeeze profit margins temporarily. If those pressures fade, some companies could recover. But losing market share for years, facing a permanent competitive disadvantage, or seeing demand structurally weaken would be much more serious. Since I’m buying index funds, I try to distinguish economy-wide shocks from structural damage to the long-term profitability of a broad range of businesses.","meaning":"","example":""}];
